Agencies have found it helpful to communicate with the public, local officials, and other stakeholders about what the cameras will be employed for and how the cameras will shape them.
Transparency about the agency’s camera policies and practices, both previous to and after implementation, can assist add to public acceptance and hold agencies accountable. Examples of transparency include posting policies on the department website and publicly releasing footage of contentious incidents.
