Sigmund Freud wrote a lot about dreams of falling teeth and even gave his own interpretation of it. He added many examples of these fears, related to sexual problems, rejection of the person we like, or simply thinking that we are not trained to face the problems of the day.
We use them to eat, to tear food apart and thus get the stomach to say it correctly. It also fulfills an aesthetic purpose: the fact of having white teeth is related to seduction, beauty, and high self-esteem.
It can also be interpreted as a fear of getting old, of losing that characteristic beauty that makes us young, it could even lead to illness. But if we dream that teeth move, then it translates as that we are surrounded by people who perhaps are not as friendly as they say they are.
Dreaming of lower teeth does not reflect the same concept. They are not as protagonists as the ones above, but we can still interpret it as that someone we appreciate may be going through a bad time.
Here we refer to the moment in which we are in front of a mirror and we see that the teeth are falling out little by little. If you dream that you see how your teeth fall out, then it means that your self-esteem is on the ground.
Although pain is common, yes you dream of the loss of a tooth and no painSo you don't have too much empathy for the people around you. So you act like you don't care too much, even though you must think they do.
It is true that when we talk about dreams about teeth, we can include them all. But if in the dream we see how a fang falls off specifically, then we bet on a new meaning.
Dreaming that your false teeth are falling out
Dreaming that your teeth are falling out can be interpreted as a regeneration process You are in a stage of maturation.
It is the indication that you have grown up and that when you were niño you had no responsibilities. The baby teeth are gone, but we would like them to come back, it will make you enjoy the innocence we had.
