What Is YouTube 360-degree Video and How Can You Benefit from It?
360-degree videos are created with the intention that viewers can interact and experience the content within, rather than just sit back and watch the video like any other regular film. Each person can choose where to look or immerse, and hence it is called an immersive video.
What is the difference between 360-degree video and virtual reality?
While both look similar, here are a few differences between the two. While the 360-degree videos offer a view from the camera’s perspective and limit the viewer’s movements to the camera’s perspective, virtual reality immerses you into a world where you can walk around.
The most vital difference is that to view a virtual reality content, you need a VR headset which is tethered or mobile, and for 360-degree content, you do not need a special device, and it can be viewed on any device that is compatible with a 360-degree video, with YouTube being the ideal platform.
YouTube 360-degree videos are a fantastic way of highlighting a brand and innovation. As a marketing expert, you must know how to strategize this feature of YouTube to your benefit.
YouTube subscribers can benefit vastly from the relatively new and upcoming feature, the 360-degree vides that offer interaction, entertainment, as well as provide information to the viewers. Considering the benefits of this feature, it leads to a lower cost per view than traditional video and keeps the viewers more engaged.
