Shop Local This Christmas – A Gift Guide To Kildare
The importance of shopping local is more evident than ever, and what more perfect time to do it than at Christmas!
The famous Irish chocolate is the brainchild of Kildare native Mary-Ann O’Brien who began mixing in her kitchen in 1992. Lily O’Brien’s are passionate about creating amazing and innovative chocolate recipes.
Looking to treat your other half, Dad, brother or mate this Christmas?
Have a night to remember this December with friends or family with a local fresh premium beer, and for those designated drivers or under 18s, don’t forget Lock 13 has a delicious three-course Christmas menu to enjoy.
From humble beginnings in County Kildare to a now global online retailer, Newbridge Silverware is a must on the Christmas list this year. The Christmas collection at the famous jewellers is now available with special designs for that special someone.
Crookstowncraft Craft Village in Kildare is a creative space for local craftspeople and those who love crafts. They stock a huge array of handmade gift items from potters, artists, felters, jewellery makers, designers, and more.
From timeless classics to head-turning must-haves, Kildare Village has mastered the art of beautiful gifting. Make KiIdare Village your one-stop shop for wish-list-worthy gifts this Christmas.
